PROVENANCE - tb/base2001.7z
===========================

base2001.7z is an overlay for tb/base.7z: 33 precompiled inputs in the object
format the 2001 port emits - big-endian ELF, e_machine 0x7262, symbol case as
written in the source. base.7z ships the same 33 paths in the format the
current port emits - big-endian ELF as well, e_machine 165 (EM_8051), symbols
uppercased by the assembler. Byte order is not what separates the two lines;
e_machine and symbol case are. `make check DATA_OVERLAY=.../base2001.7z`
unpacks base.7z and then this archive over it, so the 2.11.2 toolchain reads
inputs it understands. `make check-frozen` is that command with DATA_OVERLAY
already filled in.

Counted over every ELF image in both archives: base2001.7z holds 182 of them
(28 loose objects, 154 archive members), all EI_DATA = 2 (ELFDATA2MSB), all
e_machine 0x7262. base.7z holds 285 (30 loose, 255 members), all EI_DATA = 2;
221 carry e_machine 165 and 64 carry 0x7262 - and those 64 are the members of
lib/lib23_old/libk23.a and lib/lib23_old/libw23.a, 2001 originals kept for
comparison that no project links.

A 34th file, lib/www51.sc, rides along because the linker script names one of
those symbols; section 6 says what was done to it and why.

What a run with this overlay produces, and how it compares to the reference
ROMs base.7z ships, is recorded in the frozen report, kept with the project
documentation outside this repository.

Archive sha256: 056aed4d13749893182f9a1c4e48544ce6ce42f0e1cb85c7c6c5cf88c7d3c2ef
Archive size:   27900 bytes

tb/base.7z, which section 3 hashes into:

Archive sha256: e4cdbb943b96f589e2f072e9355e261e281c6ddcd84e529a1422d585e33163bb
Archive size:   132549 bytes

Every hash, size and count below was recomputed on 2026-09-03 by extracting
both archives and reading the bytes. Where something could not be measured
from here it says so instead of carrying a figure forward.


------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SINGLE SOURCE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every file comes from ONE place - the 2001 testbench archive, git blob

  mcs51-2.11.2-original:gnu13.tar.gz

in the backup mirror L:/ai/binutils-mcs51/backup/binutils-mcs51.git.
Retrieval, read-only:

  git fetch --depth=1 L:/ai/binutils-mcs51/backup/binutils-mcs51.git \
      mcs51-2.11.2-original
  git cat-file blob FETCH_HEAD:gnu13.tar.gz > gnu13.tar.gz
  tar xzf gnu13.tar.gz

NOT re-measured here: the blob as it sits in that mirror - this session could
reach only its own worktree. What was measured is a local copy of the same
tarball, L:/ai/binutils-mcs51/.tmp/orig/gnu13.tar.gz: 132303 bytes - the blob
size this file records - sha256
d3b27991961c6c6128b3f0dbc9f43ba187186fe3848902f411eaeb388c03658d, blob id
8733f1c5e6e6a09078e125f3d8429d296d92f7b6, 200 entries stamped 2001-01-07 to
2002-01-20. Unpacked, its gnu13/lib and gnu13/cgi copies are byte-identical to
all 33 files this overlay ships - 33 of 33, no exception.

Files are copied out of gnu13/lib and gnu13/cgi byte-for-byte. No conversion,
no repacking, no re-assembly: the tarball already holds them in the old format,
which is what the 2001 toolchain reads.

precompiled_gnu114.rar was NOT used. Measured on the local copy
L:/ai/binutils-mcs51/.tmp/orig/precompiled_gnu114.rar, 522571 bytes: 225 files
under three board/clock trees (8252/22.1184Mhz, rd2/2x20MHz, rd2/2x22.1184MHz),
each with an 80 and a 23 subtree, every member stamped 2002-09-15, after
gnu13's newest file (2002-01-20). It is a later and different build, not
another copy of the same one. Its libk80.a is 48912 bytes under
8252/22.1184Mhz/80 and 48948 under both rd2 trees, against gnu13's 42638,
because it carries 31 members to gnu13's 27: http.obj, makeipreply.obj,
smtp.obj and udpchecksum.obj are in the rar's libk80.a and in neither gnu13's
nor base.7z's. Its libw80.a likewise
carries div2x1.obj, div4x2.obj, eewrite.obj, fsearch.obj, fsend.obj and
mul2x2.obj, and lacks gnu13's div2x2.obj and http.obj. An earlier revision read
those eight names the other way round, as modules the rar was missing; the
direction above is the measured one. gnu13 supplies all 33 files the overlay
needs, including web51_80.obj and web51_23.obj, so nothing has to be filled in
from the rar.


